What is the most important OOP behavior shown by this code?

```java
final class AuditEvent {
    private final java.util.List<String> labels;
    AuditEvent(java.util.List<String> labels) { this.labels = java.util.List.copyOf(labels); }
    java.util.List<String> labels() { return labels; }
}
var source = new java.util.ArrayList<String>();
source.add("created");
var event = new AuditEvent(source);
source.add("changed");
System.out.println(event.labels().size());
```

Which option best explains the runtime behavior shown here?

